{"title":"Reverse engineering my e-scooter and rewriting the firmware in Rust","link":"https://bensimms.moe/reverse-engineering-scooter/","date":1789011124000,"content":"<a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49638071\">Comments</a><div class=\"hn-comments\"><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=kooi\">kooi</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49638434\">Sep 10, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">Very nice. Be safe out there when tweaking these things.</div><div class=\"hn-comment-children\"><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=TheChaplain\">TheChaplain</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49683062\">Sep 13, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">From what I've seen on the streets, people bypassing the restrictions will not, and there will be injuries.</div><div class=\"hn-comment-children\"><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=jstanley\">jstanley</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49683175\">Sep 13, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">You only notice the ones that aren't safe.<p>How would you know if someone bypassed the restrictions if they were riding it safely?</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=ifh-hn\">ifh-hn</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49683174\">Sep 13, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">Wish I was brainy enough to do this sort of thing!</div></div></div>","author":"","comments":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49638071","siteTitle":"Hacker News","siteHash":"37bb545430005dba450c1e40307450d8e4e791b434e83f3d38915ebad510fd50","entryHash":"fe9194fd7327380a3883e295a3975ac771e47528b82b695d7521a43a6466518a","category":"Tech"}